# A harness success is an index-1 saddle at the force stop whose endpoints pass the eOn r2205 link. The barrier window and the novelty test are catalogue counts. They do not reject a connected index-1 saddle. Failure classes are optbench.failures.apply_taxonomy.
# Of the 360 connected searches, 348 were stored as divergence. Every one of those 348 is index 1. Their force norms run from 0.00039215 to 0.00099997, so each is at the 0.001 stop. Call counts run from 823 to 2466. None missed the force stop, the Hessian index, the endpoint relaxation, or the harness cap of 20000. The old class came from the barrier window and the duplicate test. The success bit is the link. apply_taxonomy keeps those 348 as successes.
# 201 searches are not successes. apply_taxonomy names 139 wrong_stationary, 61 crash, and 1 not_converged. The 61 crashes store ErrorType.EVENT_NOT_FOUND. The not_converged search stopped on the method budget at 10000 calls, under the harness cap of 20000. None is divergence.
# fraction_eon_connected is the eOn r2205 link. Both endpoint minima are in pykmc-0.0.1-saddle-search-pt-island--pykmc-saddle-pt-smooth.endpoints.jsonl.
# The catalogue stopped 160 searches after the last new unique saddle under 1.5 eV. That saddle is search 401, barrier 1.493 eV. unique_saddles is 163. The novel saddles under 1.5 eV number 12. The sample was rescored and was not rerun.
# Potential is morse/smooth/linear. The 2014 Pt archive used shifted Morse. This row is the extra labelled sample. The baseline is pykmc/saddle-pt.
